Peter Iliff.

14
01:05:41,538 --> 01:05:47,538
It stars Patrick Swayze, Keanu Reeves, Lori Petty and Gary Busey.

15
01:10:23,076 --> 01:10:29,076
The title refers to the surfing term "point break", where a wave breaks as
it hits a point of land jutting out from the coastline.

16
01:15:04,615 --> 01:15:10,615
The film features Reeves as an undercover FBI agent who is tasked with investigating the identities of a
group of bank robbers while he develops a complex relationship with the group's leader (Swayze).

17
01:19:46,153 --> 01:19:52,153
Development of Point Break began in 1986, when Iliff
wrote an initial script for the film.

18
01:24:27,692 --> 01:24:33,692
Bigelow soon developed it with her husband, James Cameron,
and filming took place four years later.

19
01:29:09,230 --> 01:29:15,230
It was shot across the western coast of the continental
United States and was budgeted at $24 million.

20
01:33:50,769 --> 01:33:56,769
It was released on July 12, 1991.

21
01:38:32,307 --> 01:38:38,307
Point Break opened to generally positive reviews, with critics
praising the chemistry between Reeves and Swayze.

22
01:43:13,846 --> 01:43:19,846
During its theatrical run, it grossed over $83.5 million,
and has since gained a cult following.

23
01:47:55,384 --> 01:48:01,384
A remake was released in 2015.

24
